<title>USA: BPA offers Tues power during off-peak hours only.</title>
<headline>BPA offers Tues power during off-peak hours only.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) offered firm and non-firm power on Tuesday during light load hours only, the agency said Monday.</p>
<p>Firm off-peak power was offered at $9.00 per MWh for both Northwest and California-Oregon border (COB) deliveries.</p>
<p>BPA also offered non-firm power at $9.00 per MWh during hours ending 0100-0500 and 2400 PST and at $9.50 for hours ending 0600 and 2300 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 213 622 0056))</p>
</text>
